<configs>

	<!--
		=====================================================================
		 KitsuneLearnedSkills 0.4.0
		=====================================================================

		Two hidden permanent buffs, attached to the player in
		Config/entityclasses.xml:

		  buffKLSPace   the pace numbers (set from Settings.xml by the DLL).
		  buffKLSLearn  the learn-by-doing mechanism.

		=====================================================================
		 WHY THIS LIVES ON A BUFF (0.1.0 post-mortem, do not undo this)
		=====================================================================

		0.1.0 hung these effect groups off the weapon/tool ITEMS in items.xml,
		with a CVarCompare requirement at effect_group level. That crashed the
		game at XML load time: building an ItemValue runs CalcModSlotCount(),
		which evaluates item effect_group requirements with NO player entity
		present, so CVarCompare dereferenced null and killed the whole file
		parse. It silently took out recipes.xml, loot.xml, traders.xml and
		challenges.xml while reporting zero patch warnings.

		Two rules that keep us safe, both taken from vanilla's own patterns:
		  1. Live on a BUFF, not on an item. Buffs always run in player
		     context, so the item-construction path never touches us.
		  2. Put <requirement> INSIDE the <triggered_effect>, never on the
		     effect_group. Then it is only evaluated when the trigger fires.
	-->

	<!--
		=====================================================================
		 BOOTSTRAP - how the buffs get onto EXISTING characters.
		=====================================================================

		The Buffs list on the playerMale entity class is only applied when a
		character is CREATED. Existing characters load their buff list from
		their save file, so adding a buff to the class after a character
		exists does nothing for them. (Both testers' characters predate this
		mod, which is exactly how that bug was found.)

		buffStatusCheck01 is vanilla's own hidden permanent buff, attached at
		character creation since forever, so it IS in every existing save.
		Piggybacking on it re-adds our buffs on every login. AddBuff on an
		already-present buff with stack_type ignore is a no-op, so this is
		safe to fire repeatedly. New characters additionally get the buffs
		instantly from the entityclasses.xml csv append.
	-->
	<append xpath="/buffs/buff[@name='buffStatusCheck01']">
		<effect_group>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="AddBuff" buff="buffKLSPace"/>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="AddBuff" buff="buffKLSLearn"/>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfRespawn"     action="AddBuff" buff="buffKLSPace"/>
			<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfRespawn"     action="AddBuff" buff="buffKLSLearn"/>
		</effect_group>
	</append>

	<append xpath="/buffs">

		<!--
			=================================================================
			 PACE CONTROL - set it in Settings.xml (mod folder root), not here.
			=================================================================

			Each number = how many "doing" events per +1 crafting level.
			HIGHER = SLOWER. All crafting skills max at level 100.

				$kls_pace_weapon  kills while holding that weapon type
				$kls_pace_tool    block hits / repairs with that tool type
				$kls_pace_use     consumables used (food, medical)
				$kls_pace_craft   items crafted (DLL, per UnlockedBy skill)
				$kls_pace_station workstation queue completions (DLL, feeds
				                  craftingWorkstations; campfires count, so
				                  cooking is the road to the forge)
				$kls_pace_vehicle vehicle repairs (DLL, feeds craftingVehicles)
				$kls_pace_wire    wire connections (DLL, feeds craftingElectrician)
				$kls_pace_loot    fresh loot containers opened (DLL, feeds
				                  craftingBackpack)
				$kls_pace_wreck   salvage-tool hits on vehicle wrecks (feeds
				                  craftingVehicles)
				$kls_pace_harvest crops harvested (DLL, feeds craftingSeeds)
				$kls_pace_repair  armor / robotics items repaired (DLL, feeds
				                  craftingArmor / craftingRobotics)

			Since 0.8.0 the DLL REPLACES the effect group below with the
			numbers from Settings.xml (preset SLOW / MEDIUM / FAST, plus
			optional per-source overrides) while the host loads buffs.xml,
			so a dedicated server's Settings.xml is what every client gets.
			The group below is only the SLOW fallback for a missing DLL.
			Editing it does nothing while the DLL is loaded.

			Re-applied on every world entry, so a change takes effect on your
			next login, even on an existing character.

			(Editors: XML comments cannot contain a double dash, so dividers
			 here use equals signs. Keep it that way.)
		-->
		<buff name="buffKLSPace" hidden="true" remove_on_death="false">
			<stack_type value="ignore"/>

			<!-- SLOW fallback; overwritten from Settings.xml by the DLL. -->
			<effect_group>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_weapon" operation="set" value="16"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_weapon" operation="set" value="16"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_tool"   operation="set" value="80"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_tool"   operation="set" value="80"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_use"    operation="set" value="8"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_craft" operation="set" value="8"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_use"    operation="set" value="8"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_craft" operation="set" value="8"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_station" operation="set" value="16"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_station" operation="set" value="16"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_vehicle" operation="set" value="4"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_vehicle" operation="set" value="4"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_wire"    operation="set" value="4"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_wire"    operation="set" value="4"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_loot"    operation="set" value="30"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_loot"    operation="set" value="30"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_wreck"   operation="set" value="80"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_wreck"   operation="set" value="80"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_harvest" operation="set" value="24"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_harvest" operation="set" value="24"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfBuffStart"   action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_repair"  operation="set" value="8"/>
				<triggered_effect trigger="onSelfEnteredGame" action="ModifyCVar" cvar="$kls_pace_repair"  operation="set" value="8"/>
			</effect_group>

		</buff>

		<!--
			=================================================================
			 LEARN BY DOING - 16 skill lines, plus wreck salvage for Vehicles
			=================================================================

			Pattern per line (order matters, effects fire in document order):
			  1. count   the event (gated only by which item is held)
			  2. grant   +1 crafting level   (gated by held item AND threshold)
			  3. notify  the player
			  4. reset   the counter to 0    - MUST BE LAST

			Triggers used:
			  onSelfKilledOther      weapons. Solid, used by vanilla buffs.
			  onSelfDamagedBlock     harvesting + salvaging. Solid, 7 vanilla uses.
			  onSelfDestroyedBlock   salvaging: the killing blow fires this
			                         INSTEAD of onSelfDamagedBlock.
			  onSelfRepairBlock      repair tools. Fired by ItemActionRepair
			                         once per repair hit (unused in vanilla XML).
			  onSelfUpgradedBlock    repair tools, once per finished upgrade.
			  onSelfPrimaryActionEnd food + medical (the "use" half of
			                         learn-by-using). The "craft" half needs the
			                         Phase 2 DLL.

			  TriggerHasTags         on onSelfDamagedBlock checks the tags of the
			                         block that was hit (vanilla uses it for
			                         the church bell). Vehicles uses it to tell
			                         a car wreck from any other salvage hit.

			NOT COVERED HERE (handled by the DLL instead — see
			KLS_CraftLearning.cs):
			  craftingArmor, craftingRobotics    learn by crafting (UnlockedBy) and
			                                     by repairing those items
			  craftingWorkstations               workstation queue completions
			  craftingVehicles                   vehicle repairs (wreck salvage
			                                     is here, after salvagingSkill)
			  craftingElectrician                wire-tool connections
			  craftingTraps                      spikes/barbed-fence gateway crafts
			  craftingRobotics                   also pipe-baton gateway crafts
			  craftingSeeds                      farm-plot gateway crafts and
			                                     harvesting crops
			  craftingBackpack                   opening fresh loot containers
			  Armor, Backpacks and Robotics additionally keep their
			  magazines as a safety net — see Config/loot.xml.
		-->
